         <description><![CDATA[<img src='https://i.cbc.ca/ais/9c9577f7-1895-47ab-b053-1baa1e374e2c,1795637800827/full/max/0/default.jpg?im=Crop%2Crect%3D%280%2C535%2C5712%2C3213%29%3B' alt='4 residents stand in front of a cannabis store with signs opposing the store&apos;s opening. It says &quot;No cannabis near our schools. Were you notified? Neither were we. Have your say.&quot;' width='620' height='349' title='Some Meadowvale Village residents are opposing the opening of a cannabis store in their residential neighbourhood because they believe it would expose young kids to cannabis use. They also say the Alcohol and Gaming Commission of Ontario did not properly consult the community as they were supposed to.'/><p>The City of Mississauga is seeking a judicial review of the province's decision to grant a retail licence to a cannabis store in Meadowvale Village, following backlash from residents who say they weren't consulted about it.</p>]]></description>
